Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillet: a tangent ride between two crossings of the contacts: the face
between two roundings narrower than both in its middle only (mitcad#1926,
after 1721 and 1723).

A plate whose top's back edge runs past a tower of half a cylinder (its
round side towards the edge, 2 or 2.3 from it at its apex), the tower's
foot rounded with 2 (concave) and the plate's back edge with 1: their
contacts on the plate's top cross twice, the plate narrower than the two
roundings around the apex only. OCCT failed (the blends intersecting).

- ChFi3d_Builder::RideOnBlendBetweenCrossings, from Compute with 1721's
  part rides: for a pair as RideOnBlend takes them (of the other kind, or
  the smaller of one kind), the SurfData of each on the face between whose
  contacts cross twice inside both, the smaller one's contact nearer the
  other's edge between the crossings. The rider's SurfData is split at
  both crossings and its pieces before and after kept; the rider is walked
  on the larger blend's surface as a face (1721's support) over the ride's
  stretch only (its spine's range set to the crossings and a tenth beyond,
  then restored), its piece between the crossings kept, its points there
  the other pieces'; its contact on the support goes onto the face between
  (as 1720's). The larger stripe's SurfData is split at both crossings,
  its middle piece holding that contact (reversed, a curve of its own,
  where the rider runs against it). ApplyRides then makes the two blends
  meet on it as a part ride. Either stripe may have several SurfDatas.
- ChFi3d_Builder holds the stripes of such rides (myCrossingRides): their
  ends are no ends of the ride, so PerformOneCorner's and
  PerformTwoCornerAtRideEnd's tangent ride ends do not apply to them.

A rider whose spine is closed (a plate's rim rounded all round) is not
made so: a walk over a part of a periodic spine wrote past the spine's
law arrays; the pair fails as before.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_tangent_ride.cpp,
test_tower_behind_the_back_edge (ctest geometry.fillet_tangent_ride): a
half-cylinder tower 2.3 and 2.5 from the plate's back edge, its foot
rounded with 2 and the edge with 1, both orders: valid, the volume of the
two made one after the other within a millionth (the fillet failed without
the patch). It fails without the patch (shown 2026-11-20 by
tools/occt-port-proof.py, reverted together with 1725, 1727, 1728, 1729,
which change the same lines).

Failures (mitcad#1986): the rider's walk between the crossings fails with
OCCT's reports of a computation it cannot make
(ChFi3d_IsComputationFailure, 0016): the ride is undone and fails. Any
other failure (a broken invariant, a signal) is rethrown.
